  "description": "Centralized HTTP request and response logging for ASP.NET Core microservices. Publishes log entries to Apache Kafka so logs from many services can be processed in one place. Includes token-based application authentication and redaction of sensitive headers.",
  "id": "SDDP-LoggerClientNet",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-28T11:23:57.717Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "h7z9PvoS3BvoQuiyEda7e+dc4nzHcT9/SY6/ZsDxLYtdyFKXrkZGKskUOsfHzQ2jC9q13Mf4WMuUn/qrRE497A==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 49805,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/osamaeshmilh/LoggerClientNet",
  "published": "2026-11-28T11:21:50.44Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.1\n        - Metadata and documentation update. No code changes.\n        - Package title changed to \"Kafka HTTP Logger for ASP.NET Core\". The package ID is unchanged.\n        - Updated description, tags, and README.\n\n        1.1.0\n        Breaking changes. Read before upgrading from 1.0.x.\n        - The authentication method was renamed from GetApplicationIdByTokenAsync(token) to GetApplicationIdAsync(). The token now comes from configuration.\n        - All four configuration settings are required: AppToken, KafkaBootstrapServers, KafkaTopic, and AuthEndpoint. The application fails at startup if one is missing.\n        - Targets .NET 8, .NET 9, and .NET 10. .NET 6 and .NET 7 are no longer supported.\n        - response_cookies is always empty.\n\n        Fixes and changes:\n        - Request bodies are buffered, so endpoints can still read them.\n        - If authentication fails, requests pass through unlogged instead of being skipped silently.\n        - Logging errors are caught and never change the response.\n        - Sensitive headers (Authorization, Cookie, Set-Cookie, X-Api-Key) and cookie values are redacted.",
